<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Flow-GRPO</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, we formalize the iterative denoising process of flow matching models as a Markov Decision Process (MDP), denoted by the tuple <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},\rho_{0},P,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},\rho_{0},P,R)</annotation></semantics></math>. At timestep <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the state as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}\triangleq(c,t,x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}\triangleq(c,t,x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the action as the predicted next sample <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\triangleq x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\triangleq x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, the policy is given by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a_{t}\mid s_{t})\triangleq p_{\theta}(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a_{t}\mid s_{t})\triangleq p_{\theta}(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t},c)</annotation></semantics></math>. The transition dynamics are deterministic, satisfying <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(s_{t+1}\mid s_{t},a_{t})\triangleq(\delta_{c},\delta_{t-1},\delta_{x_{t-1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s_{t+1}\mid s_{t},a_{t})\triangleq(\delta_{c},\delta_{t-1},\delta_{x_{t-1}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The initial state distribution is <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}(s_{0})\triangleq(p(c),\delta_{T},\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}(s_{0})\triangleq(p(c),\delta_{T},\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the Dirac delta distribution centered at <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the reward is assigned only at the terminal step: <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(s_{t},a_{t})\triangleq r(x_{0},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(s_{t},a_{t})\triangleq r(x_{0},c)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the MDP formulation, Flow-GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> adapts the Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> algorithm to flow matching models. For each prompt <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, the policy <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math> samples a group of <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories, denoted as <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{T}^{i},x_{T-1}^{i},\dots,x_{0}^{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{T}^{i},x_{T-1}^{i},\dots,x_{0}^{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the final generated audio for the <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample. The advantage <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each sample in the group is estimated by normalizing the final rewards:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{i}=\frac{R(x_{0}^{i},c)-\text{mean}(\{R(x_{0}^{j},c)\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\text{std}(\{R(x_{0}^{j},c)\}_{j=1}^{G})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{i}=\frac{R(x_{0}^{i},c)-\text{mean}(\{R(x_{0}^{j},c)\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\text{std}(\{R(x_{0}^{j},c)\}_{j=1}^{G})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The policy is then optimized by maximizing the following surrogate objective, which averages the clipped policy gradients over the group:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\text{Flow-GRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim\mathcal{C},\{x^{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{i}(\theta)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>Flow-GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\text{Flow-GRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim\mathcal{C},\{x^{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{i}(\theta)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the per-step loss term <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{t}^{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{t}^{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{t}^{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{t}^{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\left(r_{t}^{i}(\theta)\hat{A}^{i},\text{clip}\left(r_{t}^{i}(\theta),1-\varepsilon,1+\varepsilon\right)\hat{A}^{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\left(r_{t}^{i}(\theta)\hat{A}^{i},\text{clip}\left(r_{t}^{i}(\theta),1-\varepsilon,1+\varepsilon\right)\hat{A}^{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\beta D_{\text{KL}}\left(\pi_{\theta}\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\beta D_{\text{KL}}\left(\pi_{\theta}\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the probability ratio between the current and old policies:
<math id="S2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{i}(\theta)=\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{t-1}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{i},c)}{p_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(x_{t-1}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{i},c)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{i}(\theta)=\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{t-1}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{i},c)}{p_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(x_{t-1}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{i},c)}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since GRPO requires sampling diverse audios through stochastic exploration, the standard flow-matching denoising process is inherently unsuitable as it relies on a deterministic ODE sampler:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dx_{t}=v_{\theta}(x_{t},t,c)dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dx_{t}=v_{\theta}(x_{t},t,c)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">To introduce the necessary stochasticity, Flow-GRPO converts this deterministic ODE into an equivalent SDE sampler that preserves the same marginal probability densities at all time steps. The resulting reverse-time SDE is given by:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="dx_{t}=\left(v_{t}(x_{t})-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\nabla\log p_{t}(x_{t})\right)dt+\sigma_{t}dw." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dx_{t}=\left(v_{t}(x_{t})-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\nabla\log p_{t}(x_{t})\right)dt+\sigma_{t}dw.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dw" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dw</annotation></semantics></math> denotes Wiener process increments and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=a\sqrt{\frac{t}{1-t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=a\sqrt{\frac{t}{1-t}}</annotation></semantics></math> controls the level of stochasticity during generation.
The above expression can be further transformed into:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dx_{t}=\left[v_{t}(x_{t})+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2(1-t)}(x_{t}+tv_{t}(x_{t}))\right]dt+\sigma_{t}dw." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dx_{t}=\left[v_{t}(x_{t})+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2(1-t)}(x_{t}+tv_{t}(x_{t}))\right]dt+\sigma_{t}dw.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">This continuous SDE leads to the final discretized update rule used during the transition steps:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t+\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t+\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{t,\text{mean}}+\sigma_{t}\sqrt{|\Delta t|}\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>mean</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{t,\text{mean}}+\sigma_{t}\sqrt{|\Delta t|}\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t,\text{mean}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>mean</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t,\text{mean}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{t}+\left[v_{\theta}(x_{t},t)+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2t}(x_{t}+(1-t)v_{\theta}(x_{t},t))\right]\Delta t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{t}+\left[v_{\theta}(x_{t},t)+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2t}(x_{t}+(1-t)v_{\theta}(x_{t},t))\right]\Delta t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Under this stochastic updating scheme, the transition likelihood <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x_{t-1}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{i},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x_{t-1}^{i}\mid x_{t}^{i},c)</annotation></semantics></math> utilized in the GRPO objective is explicitly defined as the Gaussian density of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,\text{mean}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>mean</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,\text{mean}}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,\text{mean}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>mean</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,\text{mean}}</annotation></semantics></math> and standard deviation <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}\sqrt{|\Delta t|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}\sqrt{|\Delta t|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By maximizing the surrogate objective <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\text{Flow-GRPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>Flow-GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\text{Flow-GRPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm effectively updates the policy model by optimizing these transition probabilities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Correlation comparison on the the PAM dataset
</span></figcaption>
<div id="S2.T2.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:59.3pt;vertical-align:-26.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(29.3pt,-5.0pt) scale(1.20489039082391,1.20489039082391) ;">
<table id="S2.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S2.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
